<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- The covered wagon from wagon_reference.png, rasterised by
     scripts/make-launcher-icon.py — read that script's header before changing the size
     here, since the number it uses is measured rather than derived.

     The short version: Wear's own circular "Recents" card avatar keeps only the
     innermost ~30% of the icon, not the ~61% Android documents as the adaptive-icon
     safe zone. At the documented size the wagon's wheels — near the bottom of its
     silhouette — were cropped off, leaving what read as flat horizontal bands rather
     than a wagon. A wheel-only icon was tried next since it's inherently round, but its
     outline is drawn in black, which is invisible against the avatar chip's own black
     background — only the orange hub survived. The wagon's white canvas and orange body
     do contrast against that background, so the wagon was kept and sized to the real
     crop instead of the documented one.

     The script fits the wagon's *minimal enclosing circle* to that crop rather than its
     bounding box: a wagon is half again as wide as it is tall and its bbox corners are
     empty, so the box overstates the room it needs and would shrink it another 10%. -->
<bitmap xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:src="@drawable/ic_launcher_wagon"
    android:gravity="center" />
